        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Video is added to a call that is already up: press the video button during a call, or the video button beside someone in Team. Linx keeps the picture small so the sound never suffers for it, and turns it off by itself if the connection gets too slow.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 21,
          "startingLine": 64
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Start video calls with the front camera",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 24,
          "startingLine": 62
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Video",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 22,
          "startingLine": 69
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Appearance",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 24,
          "startingLine": 73
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Appearance",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 22,
          "startingLine": 81
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "On, a Linx call sits in the iPhone's own Recents beside your ordinary calls, and you can tap one to ring it back from there. Off, Linx keeps its calls to itself — the Calls tab still has every one of them. Calls already made stay where they are.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 21,
          "startingLine": 88
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Show Linx calls in the Phone app",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 24,
          "startingLine": 85
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Your call history",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 22,
          "startingLine": 93
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Notifications",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 32,
          "startingLine": 100
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Notification settings",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 28,
          "startingLine": 102
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Turn notifications on",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 28,
          "startingLine": 108
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "How calls arrive here",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 22,
          "startingLine": 117
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "A call rings this phone whether the app is open or not. Notifications are for the quieter things: a missed call and a new voicemail. Closing the app is fine — your extension shows as offline between calls, and Linx wakes the phone when someone rings you.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 21,
          "startingLine": 120
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Sign out of this phone",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 24,
          "startingLine": 129
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Signing out forgets this phone's key. If you've lost the phone, stop it in Linx on a computer: My account → My phones → I've lost it.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 21,
          "startingLine": 132
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Sign out",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 20,
          "startingLine": 142
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Keep me signed in",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 20,
          "startingLine": 145
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "This phone will stop ringing, and you'll need a new setup code to use it again.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 18,
          "startingLine": 147
        }
